From 770e2c6b5a331d75c1dbe646a91e80086008d2dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41(tilelang): parallelize fused mHC finalize across tile
 CTAs for M<=16

Hoist load_split_tf32 before the stream fold in project_and_finalize_streams
to match project_streams, split atomic arrival into mhc_claim and mhc_wait_splits
with nanosleep backoff so the last live_m split CTAs finalize one token each in
parallel across live_m SMs while the first 40 - live_m CTAs exit early, place
pdl.trigger() after mhc_claim and preload scale/base/weight during the split
wait, unroll the 24-lane S/P and 96-thread Q split reductions in fixed split
order, raise FINALIZE_FUSE_MAX_ROWS from 1 to 16, and pre-allocate split
counters up to max(FINALIZE_FUSE_MAX_ROWS, max_num_batched_tokens).

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: After vLLM 0634 optimized standalone project_streams and finalize,
project_and_finalize_streams still kept FINALIZE_FUSE_MAX_ROWS = 1, unhoisted
load_split_tf32, early pdl.chain(), and a single-CTA serial loop over all 16
tile rows with un-unrolled split loops (124 IKET events/warp at iters=2).
Parallelizing Stage 2 across live_m split CTAs eliminates the second kernel
launch across M = 1..16 while cutting IKET iters=2 bound from 124 to 90 and
fitting iters=1 within <= 60 events/warp (28..30 sites) with zero register
spills on SM121.
Quality implications: None; 100% bit-identical FP32/BF16/MXFP8 arithmetic and
outputs to project_streams + finalize in fixed split order 0..splits-1 on
finite and non-finite inputs.
Tests: tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_mhc.py and SM121 CPU compile,
PDL, and IKET static bound checks across all 10 kernel variants.
Upstream status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang kernel optimization; candidate
for upstreaming to local-inference-lab/vllm.
